      "title": "White House blocks CNN from Air Force One in latest escalation with news media",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/25/white-house-cnn-air-force-one",
      "description": "<p>Outlet had been scheduled to fly with Donald Trump to Tennessee for a college football game, network said Friday</p><p>The White House has blocked CNN from traveling aboard Air Force One on Saturday, impeding its TV press pool duties in the latest escalation of the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/media/2026/sep/25/trump-media-ban-white-house-pool\">administration’s battle</a> with the news media.</p><p>CNN had been scheduled to fly with Donald Trump to Tennessee for a college football game, the network said on <a href=\"https://www.cnn.com/2026/09/25/politics/white-house-blocks-cnn-air-force-one-travel-pool\">Friday</a>. The White House confirmed CNN’s exclusion when it did not list the network on guidance sent to the press corps regarding Trump’s schedule for Saturday.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/25/white-house-cnn-air-force-one\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-26T12:45:33"
    },
    {
      "title": "CNN left off Air Force One as Trump admin signals new media restriction",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/cnn-left-off-air-force-one-as-trump-admin-signals-new-media-restriction-126092600106_1.html",
      "description": "The White House signalled Friday night that CNN would be left off Air Force One for President Donald Trump's Saturday trip, the latest media restriction from the administration in an ongoing dispute with First Amendment implications.\nThe news organisation was replaced by Real America's Voice News, a conservative outlet.\nThe news came just after journalists from three news outlets that Trump banned last week from the White House grounds returned to the executive complex with TV cameras, laptops and microphones in hand.\nThe US network video pool for the White House was back in operation Friday, for the first time since President Donald Trump banned three news outlets in an extraordinary showdown over media access.\nAt noon on CNN, viewers could see Trump and President Xi Jinping touring the National Archives, along with Melania Trump and Peng Liyuan, Xi's wife. The banner along the bottom of the screen read: \"Trump and China's Xi Visit National Archives.\" It was a routine report from",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-26T02:08:33"
    }
